<title>USA: Entergy files stranded nuke cost with Texas.</title>
<headline>Entergy files stranded nuke cost with Texas.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entergy Corp, seeking to smooth the road to retail electric competition without hurting its customers, said it will file a plan Wednesday with Texas to recover costs linked to its River Bend nuclear plant.</p>
<p>The 936 megawatt plant serves customers in Texas and Louisiana.</p>
<p>&quot;This plan creates an orderly transition process to bring about a competitive marketplace in seven years,&quot; Entergy executive vice president of external affairs, Jerry Jackson said Tuesday in a news release.</p>
</text>
